WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:05.715
Plans change after a Popkin starts. Now the Host can change it too.

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:11.235
Mara hosts Lakeside Weekend. In Popkin settings she has four choices: edit the name

00:00:11.235 --> 00:00:15.508
and look, change how long it lasts, invite people, and wrap up.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.875
The weekend is running long. She renames it Lakeside Long Weekend, picks the party

00:00:20.875 --> 00:00:22.126
popper and plum.

00:00:22.326 --> 00:00:25.788
She saves, and the home shows the new name and colour at once.

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:33.358
Clear the name, and the field asks you to give your Popkin a name.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:41.034
How long should it last? The weekend is chosen, so she picks Until a date: Monday at

00:00:41.034 --> 00:00:41.574
six.

00:00:41.774 --> 00:00:44.607
The time left now reads two days, six hours.

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:54.758
And everyone sees it. On another member's screen, the name, the colour and the time

00:00:54.758 --> 00:00:56.720
left change without a reload.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.229
In the last hour, the Host's Change on the banner opens the same choice.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.079
On a phone, the dialog is a sheet from the bottom.

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:16.264
On a bigger screen, it sits in the middle.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.960
What no screen shows: only the Host may change it, a wrapped-up Popkin can't be

00:01:26.960 --> 00:01:30.524
changed, and a late change never undoes a newer one.

00:01:30.724 --> 00:01:33.381
Still to come: the Popkin's own address.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:38.834
That is journey sixteen. Popkin is a free platform for pop-up communities.
